 {"id": "DOC-14", "title": "P5 — README --version example 'off-by-one 0287082' matches no build mode (source build prints 0.3.0-dev; release ldflags inject the tag)", "status": "pending", "priority": "P5", "complexity": 1, "created_at": "2026-11-23T19:26:28Z", "updated_at": "2026-11-23T19:26:28Z", "capability_tags": [], "created_by": null, "detail": {"metadata": {}, "fingerprint": "512ef96f89871e37ce27655ba2a8a78b416b10ce35b3ae4d599314daafa013ad"}, "reasoning": "Taxonomy: rot (stale example literal in a documented command's output claim). README.md:330, the Command-Line Flags table (### Command-Line Flags, slug #command-line-flags), documents `--version` as \"Print the build stamp (e.g. `off-by-one 0287082`) and exit\". T3 probe on a fresh build from HEAD a9c9f4d0 (go build -o /tmp/oobo-docs-r2-bin ./cmd/off-by-one; /tmp/oobo-docs-r2-bin --version): prints `off-by-one 0.3.0-dev`. Source of truth: cmd/off-by-one/main.go:52-53 — `var version = \"0.3.0-dev\"`, \"overridden at build time via -ldflags \\\"-X main.version=...\\\"\"; the CHANGELOG v0.2.0/v0.3.0 prep notes state release builds inject the TAG, so a release artifact prints e.g. `off-by-one v0.3.0`. No build mode prints a bare hex stamp; grep '0287082' across README/docs/skills returns only README.md:330. A developer comparing their build's output against the README example concludes the stamping is broken when it is not. Reader: developer/operator. Doc severity is P5 by fleet ruling 2026-09-30 (polish; P4/P5 only, never P1-P3). Filed by the R2 pass of tick off-by-one-docs-2026-11-23-18-36-23 (second instance). Evidence: .coding-hermes/board/evidence/2026-11-23-docs-audit/probe-transcript.txt section H (pre-append digest 2619400fea7dfa606121677b616859e0fc06508760df591847b353b4007b8f22 = first-pass bytes at a9c9f4d0).\n\nch:trace row=DOC-14 spec=README.md#command-line-flags doc=README.md evidence=.coding-hermes/board/evidence/2026-11-23-docs-audit/probe-transcript.txt witness=none:ephemeral-fresh-build-captured